<section id="about">
  <SectionHeading
    number="01"
    title="About the Competition"
    subtitle="An individual competitive programming tournament hosted at Bergen County Academies."
  />

  <p>
    The <strong>Daniel H. Plotnick Memorial Computing Competition (DHPMCC)</strong> is an in-person programming competition hosted at <strong>Bergen County Academies</strong> in Hackensack, New Jersey.
  </p>
  <p>
    DHPMCC is structured as an individual algorithmic contest. Competitors are presented with a series of original, rigorous computer science problems and are tasked with formulating and implementing optimal solutions under fixed contest constraints.
  </p>
  <p>
    The competition emphasizes deep algorithmic reasoning, time complexity optimization, and rigorous implementation over trivial coding tasks. Solutions are evaluated automatically against comprehensive sets of secret test cases on an isolated judging server.
  </p>
</section>
